s://api.github.com/repos/boschresearch/pandas/commits/c82d0fb52ecece0f183f33f08fabef43a2341f83","created_at":"2022-04-07T06:47:08Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/comments/1091352600","html_url":"https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/46658#issuecomment-1091352600","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/46658","id":1091352600,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAA0YD85BDLgY","user":{"login":"johannes-mueller","id":5902745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDI3NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5902745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes-mueller","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-04-07T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2022-04-07T08:56:08Z","body":"I addressed this issue in a PR. I would probably need some help with the following questions\r\n\r\n* How to fix [this error](https://dev.azure.com/pandas-dev/pandas/_build/results?buildId=76292&view=logs&j=915dbb23-6529-54ae-059d-ec0b59ba10e8&t=86b091c2-17fe-52fe-2454-5f56a371e155&l=1669)\r\n  `subset` in [this line](https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/blob/c82d0fb52ecece0f183f33f08fabef43a2341f83/pandas/_libs/intervaltree.pxi.in#L381) is a `int64_t` array and originates from an `Int64Vector`. So I understand why the cast to the 32bit `size_t` is considered unsafe. But I don't understand why the failure occurs only in my tests.\r\n\r\n* Is the [way I am calculating the pivot](https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas/pull/46664/files#diff-0cdcd399d6b4bc9a8a3540ad21e52195ee7fb74e8c87a6f0b1a4675e3ae06395R327) actually correct? It works for the cases that I had IRL. But I can still easily trigger the infinite recursion using the internal `IntervalTree` e.g. when `left` of an `IntervalTree` completely contains `right` like `IntervalTree([-2., 2.] * 101, [-1, 1] * 101)`\r\n\r\nIt would be helpful to have some discussion about that.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/comments/1091352600/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"johannes-mueller","id":5902745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5MDI3NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5902745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes-mueller","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes-mueller/received_events","type":"User","user_vi